    "display_title": "chore(ci): split the scaling check by stage and the digests by set",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "chore/ci-split-scaling-and-digests",
    "head_commit_message": "chore(ci): split the scaling check by stage and the digests by set\n\nThe scaling check was the slowest job in both workflows, the digests the\nnext. Each stage of the scaling check (march, fight, stacks) now runs as\nits own job, with all its sizes timed on one machine, since its growth\nratios only hold within one machine; scaling_check.gd takes stages= to\npick them. Each digest set runs as its own job, comparing its own two\nengines.\n\nPushes to main failed run-baseline: a push checks out the branch itself,\nso base_ref.py skipped origin/main and compared against the nearest other\nbranch, counting 97 files the push didn't change. A push now compares\nagainst the commit before it (Decision 50).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D25MB57Z7nmE6u7pDpd3yj",
    "head_sha": "1453a193eb5517bd6eee83f556bd02fd52824eb8",
